{"type":"WebSearch","query":"California Prop 1 2026 early results election day","content":"**California Proposition 1 (2026) is a legislatively referred bond measure on the November 3, 2026, general election ballot.** It would authorize the state to issue $11.25 billion in general obligation bonds for housing affordability programs, including multifamily rental housing, veterans’ mortgages (CalVet home loans), supportive housing, preservation of existing affordable units, down-payment assistance, farmworker/tribal/student housing, and related infrastructure. A yes vote allows the borrowing (repaid over about 25 years at an estimated $500–600 million annually from the General Fund for the main portion); a no vote does not. It requires a simple majority to pass.[[1]](https://voterguide.sos.ca.gov/propositions/1/title-summary.htm)

**Unofficial election-night results are not yet available.** The California Secretary of State’s results site currently shows 0% of precincts reporting and 0 votes tallied for Proposition 1 (and all other statewide measures), with a note to check back after 8:00 p.m. Pacific Time on Election Night (Tuesday, November 3, 2026) for live updates. Vote-by-mail, provisional, and other ballots will continue to be counted afterward; official certification is expected by December 11, 2026. News outlets tracking the race (such as KCRA) also have placeholders for results that will populate after polls close.[[2]](https://electionresults.sos.ca.gov/)

Pre-election polling (e.g., PPIC surveys) showed the measure leading, with yes support around 55–60% among likely voters in September–October 2026, and independent forecasts giving it a very high chance of passage. There was no organized opposition campaign with reported contributions. For the latest unofficial results once they start coming in, visit the official California Secretary of State election results page.","citations":["https://voterguide.sos.ca.gov/propositions/1/title-summary.htm","https://electionresults.sos.ca.gov/"],"allowed_domains":null}
